4.1 LRI shall submit to the Board's Monitoring and Evaluation Unit:
(a) a weekly field activity report, due every Monday by 12:00 noon WAT for the preceding week;
(b) a monthly narrative report, due on the 5th day of the following month;
(c) a quarterly financial expenditure report, due within 10 Working Days after the end of each quarter.

4.2 All reports shall be submitted in both hard copy and electronic format to the designated Contract Officer.

4.3 The Board shall acknowledge receipt of each report within 5 Working Days. Failure to submit any report on time shall constitute a breach of this Agreement.

**5. DATA SUBMISSION VIA HOTS**

5.1 LRI shall capture and transmit all service delivery data through the Health Outreach Tracking System (HOTS).

5.2 Data entries shall be made in real time at the point of service, or within 24 hours of the outreach session where connectivity is unavailable.

5.3 The minimum data fields required for each beneficiary encounter are:
(a) unique beneficiary identifier;
(b) age and sex;
(c) service type;
(d) date and location of service;
(e) referral status (if any).

5.4 LRI shall ensure that all CHVNs are trained on HOTS usage prior to the first outreach session and shall maintain a log of training attendance.

5.5 The Board may conduct random spot checks of HOTS data against physical registers. Any significant discrepancy, as determined by the Board in its sole discretion, shall be treated as a breach of this Agreement.

**6. SUBCONTRACTOR OVERSIGHT**

6.1 LRI shall not subcontract any part of the services without the prior written approval of the Board.

6.2 Where subcontracting is approved, LRI shall:
(a) ensure that any subcontractor agrees in writing to comply with the terms of this Agreement;
(b) remain fully liable for the performance of any subcontractor;
(c) provide the Board with a copy of each subcontract agreement.

1.1 Clause 9.1 of the Agreement is hereby amended to extend the term of the Agreement for a further period of twelve (12) months. The revised term shall commence on the 1st day of February 2023 and shall continue in force until the 31st day of January 2024, unless terminated earlier in accordance with the provisions of the Agreement, as amended by this Addendum.

**2. EXPANSION OF SERVICE SCOPE**

2.1 The Parties agree to expand the service scope from ten (10) LGAs to twelve (12) LGAs, with the addition of Ibeju-Lekki and Epe Local Government Areas.

2.2 The expanded scope of services shall include the following additional activities in the newly added LGAs:
(a) Community mobilization and health education sessions on maternal, newborn, and child health (MNCH) and family planning;
(b) Distribution of long-lasting insecticidal nets (LLINs) in coordination with the National Malaria Elimination Programme;
(c) Support for routine immunization outreach sessions at fixed and temporary posts;
(d) Referral of complicated cases to secondary health facilities, with documentation of referral outcomes.

2.3 All other terms and conditions of the Agreement relating to the provision of services shall apply mutatis mutandis to the expanded scope, save where expressly amended herein.

**3. REVISED REPORTING AND DATA OBLIGATIONS**

3.1 Clause 8.11 of the Agreement is hereby amended to require LRI to submit the following reports to the Board's Monitoring & Evaluation (M&E) Unit:

(a) **Monthly Activity Reports**: to be submitted no later than the 5th day of the following month, detailing all outreach activities conducted, including location, date, number of beneficiaries reached, and types of services provided;

(b) **Quarterly Performance Reports**: to be submitted no later than 15 days after the end of each quarter, providing a detailed analysis of performance against the approved work plan, including challenges encountered and corrective actions taken;

(c) **End-of-Programme Report**: to be submitted no later than 30 days after the expiration or termination of the Agreement, providing a comprehensive summary of all activities, outputs, outcomes, and lessons learned.

