3.2 All reports shall be submitted in both hard copy and electronic format, and shall be accompanied by relevant supporting documentation, including attendance registers, service delivery logs, and distribution records.

3.3 LRI shall ensure that all data submitted to the Board's M&E Unit is accurate, complete, and verifiable. The Board reserves the right to conduct spot checks and verification exercises to validate the data submitted.

**4. HEALTH OUTCOME TRACKING SYSTEM (HOTS) DATA REQUIREMENTS**

4.1 The Parties agree that LRI shall collect and submit data into the Board's Health Outcome Tracking System (HOTS) in accordance with the following requirements:

(a) LRI shall designate a Data Focal Person who shall be responsible for the timely and accurate entry of all required data into HOTS;

(b) Data shall be entered into HOTS within five (5) working days of the completion of each outreach session;

(c) The minimum dataset to be entered into HOTS shall include: date of session, LGA, ward, facility/community location, type of service delivered, number of beneficiaries disaggregated by sex and age group, number of referrals made, and any other data fields as may be specified by the Board from time to time;

(d) LRI shall participate in quarterly data review meetings convened by the Board to discuss HOTS data quality, completeness, and utilization.

4.2 The Board shall provide LRI with access credentials and user training for HOTS within thirty (30) days of the effective date of this Addendum.
